text:
nora: Quick note from today's console pass ":dark_mode:" — small-token legibility + chart hierarchy still tripping up a few flows. Posting screenshots in the PR.

chuck: Can you call out the failure cases?

nora: 1) 11px model tags in tables disappear on low-brightness monitors. 2) Multi-series sparkline rows lose the tertiary series entirely. 3) keyboard focus on small buttons is almost invisible.

jamal: Might we try micro-contrast backplates for tokens instead of globally brightening text? preserves mood.

soph: For charts, add a visual hierarchy: base palette (desaturated) + two accent slots for important series. Also add tiny markers at data points so thin lines show up.

nora: Agree. Draft variables in CSS: ```css
:root[data-theme=dark] {
  --panel: #071217;
  --token-base: #dfe9ee;
  --token-backdrop: rgba(10,16,20,0.34);
  --chart-base: #4a90a8, #6fb3a2, #7fbf8a;
  --chart-accents: #ffd05a, #ff7a7a;
}
```

chuck: Love the backdrop idea. Can we scope it to `.token-inline` and `.table-badge` only? keeps body text unchanged.

jamal: Also add `stroke-dasharray` patterns for chart lib when >4 series. Good for b/w prints.

soph: I'll draft a tiny11px reading task for 10 users: copy the inline model id, identify "throughput" series on a 6-line chart.

theme-bot: Preview deployed by @nora: https://staging.redwood-inference.internal/preview/obsidian-ink-1809 — includes token backplates, marker-enabled charts, and focus ring tweaks.

nora: Thanks all ":thumbsup:" I'll push the PR with screenshots, test plan, and CSS.
